{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":30373123,"ns":0,"title":"Amitsur–Levitzki theorem","extract":"In algebra, the Amitsur–Levitzki theorem states that the algebra of n × n matrices over a commutative ring satisfies a certain identity of degree 2n. It was proved by Amitsur and  Levitsky (1950).","description":"States that the algebra of n by n matrices satisfies a certain identity of degree 2n","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}